  "ingredients": [
    "4 tablespoon butter",
    "1/4 medium onion",
    "2 teaspoon ruled.me roasted garlic",
    "1/2 teaspoon fresh ginger",
    "1/2 teaspoon salt",
    "1/2 teaspoon black pepper",
    "1/4 teaspoon ground cinnamon",
    "1/4 teaspoon ground coriander",
    "1/8 teaspoon ground nutmeg",
    "1 whole bay leaf",
    "1 cup pumpkin puree",
    "1 1/2 cup chicken broth",
    "4 ounce bacon",
    "1/2 cup heavy whipping cream"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "In a large saucepan over medium-low heat, add the butter and let it melt completely. You want it to take on a golden color.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spiced-pumpkin-soup/#wprm-recipe-51281-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1548.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dice the onion and mince the garlic and fresh ginger.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spiced-pumpkin-soup/#wprm-recipe-51281-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1553.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a small container, mix the salt, pepper, cinnamon, coriander, nutmeg, and bay leaf.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spiced-pumpkin-soup/#wprm-recipe-51281-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1558.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the butter has turned a dark golden color, add the onion, garlic, and ginger to the pan and stir well. Sauté for about 2–3 minutes, or until the onions are becoming translucent.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spiced-pumpkin-soup/#wprm-recipe-51281-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1571.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Measure out the pumpkin puree and set aside.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spiced-pumpkin-soup/#wprm-recipe-51281-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1574.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the onions are translucent, add the spices to the pan and let cook for 1–2 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spiced-pumpkin-soup/#wprm-recipe-51281-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1584.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the pumpkin puree and mix it in with the onions and spices.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spiced-pumpkin-soup/#wprm-recipe-51281-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1589.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the chicken broth and stir to combine.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spiced-pumpkin-soup/#wprm-recipe-51281-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1601.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bring to a boil and then reduce the heat to low and let simmer for 20 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spiced-pumpkin-soup/#wprm-recipe-51281-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1607.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once simmered remove bay leaf, then use an immersion blender to blend all of the remaining ingredients together. You want a smooth puree here, so make sure you take your time. Cook for an additional 20 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spiced-pumpkin-soup/#wprm-recipe-51281-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1614.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Meanwhile, cook the bacon over medium heat in a separate pan. You can use a splatter guard to keep from making a mess on your stovetop.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spiced-pumpkin-soup/#wprm-recipe-51281-step-0-10",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1622.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the soup is ready, pour in the heavy cream and grease from your cooked bacon. Stir to combine.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spiced-pumpkin-soup/#wprm-recipe-51281-step-0-11",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/img_1627.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Crumble the bacon over the soup and serve. Optional: Garnish with chopped parsley and a bit of sour cream.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spiced-pumpkin-soup/#wprm-recipe-51281-step-0-12",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
